.Dd July 27, 2026
.Dt SECUREARC-TESTKEY 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm securearc-testkey
.Nd verify ARC DNS key record matches local private key
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Fl s Ar selector
.Fl d Ar domain
.Fl k Ar keyfile
.Op Fl n Ar nameserver
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
fetches an ARC public key from DNS and verifies that it matches the
specified local private key file.
ARC uses the same DNS key format and location as DKIM
.Pq Ar selector Ns ._domainkey. Ns Ar domain .
.Pp
Use this to confirm that DNS records are correctly published before
enabling ARC sealing.
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Fl s Ar selector
ARC selector name.
Required.
.It Fl d Ar domain
Domain name.
Required.
.It Fl k Ar keyfile
Path to the private key file to compare against.
Required.
.It Fl n Ar nameserver
DNS nameserver IP address for the lookup.
Default:
.Dq 127.0.0.1 .
.It Fl h
Display usage information.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Bl -tag -width indent -compact
.It 0
Key matches \(em DNS public key corresponds to the local private key.
.It 1
Key mismatch or DNS lookup failure.
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Bd -literal -offset indent
securearc-testkey -s arc2026 -d bambania.com -k /usr/local/etc/securearc/arc.key
securearc-testkey -s arc2026 -d example.com -k /path/to/arc.key -n 8.8.8.8
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr securearc 8 ,
.Xr securedkim-genkey 8
.Sh AUTHORS
.An Daniel Morante
